okay so now we've learned about what  automatic dlp is we've configured it and  it's running creating our data profiles  now we get to the fun part analyzing the  results  welcome to another video about automatic  data loss prevention or dlp if you  haven't been following along check out  this playlist for our earlier videos  data is only as good as the insights  you're able to get from it and  oftentimes we have the data we can see  it  but we have to do a lot of work to  actually get to those useful insights  thankfully automatic dlp has a few easy  ways to write and consume the results of  your scans  you can use the console publish to  chronicle export profiles to bigquery  which will allow you to run sql queries  and visualize the profiles in data  studio and publish notifications to pub  sub  let's touch on each of these a little  deeper and take a look at some examples  the simplest way to consume your data is  right in the console  so once you save your configuration  click on the profiles tab and your  information is right there in the table  here you can see your bigquery assets  and filter by projects data sets and  tables you can also click on a specific  table to see the full table profile  along with a list of all the column  profiles for that table  also included are links to access logs  iim recommendations access lists and  more  publishing to chronicle is a powerful  feature that can bring your sensitive  data insights into your security  operations to enrich your threat  detection investigation and response  the chronicle platform allows security  teams to cost effectively store and  analyze all their security data in one  place to investigate and detect threats  at speed and scale  by sending your data to chronicle you're  enhancing your security operations and  improving your overall posture  to use this feature chronicle must be  enabled for your organization  you can also choose to export your data  to bigquery this will allow you access  to your data in its raw form but in a  queryable format you can write sql  queries against it or load the data into  a third-party tool of your choice  to export your data profiles to bigquery  you'll need the project id data set id  and table id of the table where you want  the profiles to be exported to let's  call this the output table  i created a project lovely lion data set  and table in bigquery before this so  i'll use that here  okay so now we save and we can go check  out our results in bigquery  when automatic dlp exports data profiles  to your output table it also creates the  latest view this view is a pre-filtered  virtual table that includes only the  latest snapshots of your data profiles  the output table contains all the older  snapshots of the data profile in case  you want to see change history or keep  an audit  the latest view has the same schema as  the output table so you can choose the  two interchangeably  the query results will differ though  because the output table contains  historical data  okay now let's check our data  i want to query my data set for person  names to do that i select the table i  want demo table 1  and click query  i'll delete the first line and then put  in a sample query you can find some of  these sample queries in the  documentation  customize the sample query to use the  table you want to query  in this case i'm actually going to go  with the latest view table  and then click run  the results appear and there you can see  every table across my organization that  has a column containing person names  org level scans will pull from all  projects in the org so you'll see my  project lovely lion and the other  projects that my colleagues have made  so that is how you can query your data  by publishing two bigquery from dlp  having the power of bigquery enables you  to analyze the data however you need it  also means you can create visual  dashboards and reports and tools like  data studio or looker  to get you started we provided a  pre-made as in made for you data studio  report that highlights the rich insights  of your data  data studio is a report generation tool  that enables users to easily visualize  their data  you can use this pre-made report as is  or you can customize it as needed  to view the pre-made report with your  data enter the required values for  project id data set id and table or view  id in the following url  then copy the resulting url to your  browser for the purpose of showing you  the best dashboard possible i'm going to  use some more robust data than the test  data that i put in my data set and this  is what it will look like when you have  all your data loaded  the automatic data profiler dashboard is  a multi-page report that gives you a  quick high-level view of your data  profiles including breakdowns by risk by  info type and by location  and you can explore the other tabs to  drill down to specific metrics like  regional summary  and advanced exploration  this allows you to quickly see answers  to specific questions like do i have pii  in europe  cool  and if you do want to create a custom  report with your data you can  check out the documentation in the  description for instructions  another option is to publish to pub sub  this option lets you provide pub sub  topics to send notifications about and  when to send those notifications  like when a table is reprofiled or when  the risk or sensitivity score of a table  increases  you choose what criteria will generate a  notification and whether the  notification should include just the  affected table's resource name or the  full table profile  these alerts will make you aware of any  possible risk in your data as soon as  it's found so that you can take  necessary actions quickly  now you can see why automatic dlp allows  you to easily get rich insights from  your data with the options we've  discussed you can now look at your data  in a more in-depth way than previously  possible and these features expand  opportunities for you and your business  make sure you check out the links in the  description for documentation and in our  next video we'll talk about what to do  with your findings to remediate issues  and mitigate risk  thanks for watching  you
 

